  python  repr(float), str(float), float.__repr__, float.__str__
  note    the fewest digits that read back, and the nearest of them, with no exponent or in exponent form; the language's `to_str` promises only that its text reads back, and writes 2 to the -778th in 17 digits where 16 do (runtime/parts/f64.c says "shortest is not promised"); Python's `repr`, Go's `g` with -1 and Rust's `Debug` each choose between the two forms by their own thresholds, and `to_str` by its; a whole value ends ".0" as `to_str` writes it, where Go and Rust's Display write none; 11,926 cases against Go's `f` and `e` with -1, 5,963 values each written both ways, every power of two of both widths among them, 0 disagreeing

